Hi Pavel (or others), 

I was still waiting for a response on a couple of issues. I've synthesized them below. Would love an answer! 

Thanks

Juan
@juancommander 

1) 

How do you set up a valued network with the network package for the ergm.count module to understand? The documentation I have for the network package does not mention weighted networks explicitly. I've tried loading an adjacency matrix with values and adding a "weight" edge attribute with no success. 

What edge attribute does ergm.count expect for the edge values? 

Potentially related: 
When I try to use a valued version of the "mutual" ergm-term, I am seeing the following error: 
Error: mutual model term does not recognize form argument

2)  

I am trying to write my own userterm to do a nodematch, but with a different definition of what it means to match. I want to match if two of the categories share a 2-character substring (instead of matching 100%). 

I have made progress: I have defined my userterm, its being loaded, but I am having a hard time figuring out the C code for what I want to do. 

I am borrowing code from d_nodematch, but I have a question (added in a comment below).

/*****************
 changestat: d_nodematchsubstr
*****************/
CHANGESTAT_FN(d_nodematchsubstr) {
  double matchval;
  Vertex tail, head, ninputs;
  int i, j, edgeflag;

  ninputs = N_INPUT_PARAMS - N_NODES;

  /* *** don't forget tail -> head */
  ZERO_ALL_CHANGESTATS(i);
  FOR_EACH_TOGGLE(i) {
    tail=TAIL(i);
    head=HEAD(i);
    matchval = INPUT_PARAM[tail+ninputs-1];

    //
    // what is the type of matchval here? 
    // how do I get at the String of this attribute for my head and tail nodes? 
    //  

    if (matchval == INPUT_PARAM[head+ninputs-1]) { /* We have a match! */
      edgeflag = IS_OUTEDGE(tail, head);
      if (ninputs==0) {/* diff=F in network statistic specification */
        CHANGE_STAT[0] += edgeflag ? -1.0 : 1.0;
      } else { /* diff=T */
        for (j=0; j<ninputs; j++) {
          if (matchval == INPUT_PARAM[j])
            CHANGE_STAT[j] += edgeflag ? -1.0 : 1.0;
        }
      }
    }
    TOGGLE_IF_MORE_TO_COME(i);
  }
  UNDO_PREVIOUS_TOGGLES(i);
} 

